   stem \tab en \tab es \cr
   \code{"primary"} \tab What is the PRIMARY subject of this text? \tab \enc{¿Cuál}{Cual} es el tema PRINCIPAL de este texto? \cr
   \code{"best"} \tab Which category best describes this text? \tab \enc{¿Qué categoría}{Que categoria} describe mejor este texto? \cr
}


They are not interchangeable. \code{"primary"} asks what the text is about, which
assumes the categories are subjects. \code{"best"} asks which category describes
it, which assumes only that they are a scheme worth sorting into. Any other
string is used as the question verbatim, in whatever language it is written.
